  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only existing task-level search, approach, claim, release, pickup, drop, publication, color-observation, confirmation, and team-reception events needed to deliver the nine boxes. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because motion safety and collision recovery remain governed by the fixed free-behavior plants and collision_avoidance.",
    "transition_design": "R3_Search through R1_Publish enforce three one-box red batches; G3_Search through G3_Publish enforce a two-box green batch and G1_Search through G1_Publish enforce the final one-box batch; B3_Search through B3_Publish enforce one three-box blue batch. Search and approach actions are repeatable self-loops, visibility loss returns to the matching search state, reached observations gate pickup or drop, failures recover through release or renewed zone search, and claim-attempt states abandon their attempt on the matching received_claim event. Matching received_delivered events update the active completed-batch count. Only AllDelivered is marked, and no low-level motion action is constrained by this specification.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
}
